# Carbon (Neon rewrite)

`carbon/` is a step-by-step, clean-architecture rewrite of the Neon multi-GPU grid library. Read
`AGENTS.md` at the repo root for the full brief, status, and gap analysis. Key invariants:

- `Neon/` is vendored **read-only** reference. Do not modify it. The rewrite lives in the
  `carbon::` namespace under `include/carbon/`, `src/`, `tests/`.
- Current focus: port Neon's `dGrid` data plane. Foundations in place: `DataView`,
  `Integer3d<T>` / `Floating3d<T>` and aliases (`int32_3d`, `int64_3d`, `float32_3d`,
  `float64_3d`), `Idx`, `Span` (owns `z_offset` and `linear_offset` math), `Partition<T, N>`
  with `read(span, idx, component_id)`.

## Style (enforced by `.clang-format`)

- **Divided signature style**, applied to *every* function:
  ```cpp
  [[nodiscard]] CARBON_HD constexpr auto
  name(Arg1 a,
       Arg2 b) const noexcept -> RetType;
  ```
  Return type + qualifiers on line 1, function name on line 2, one parameter per line stacked
  under the first. Applies even to 2-param functions. `BinPackParameters: AlwaysOnePerLine`,
  `BreakAfterReturnType: All`.
- Types PascalCase; functions / members snake_case; enum enumerators PascalCase; enum string forms
  lowercase.
- Prefer bare `int64_t` over `std::int64_t`.
- Constructor init lists always stacked; access modifiers flush with class body; no comment
  reflow; no narration comments.

## Workflow

After any substantive edit, run all three and do not stop until they're clean:

```bash
cmake --build build -j
ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure
cmake --build build --target format-check
```

`clang-format` 20+ must be on PATH (`pip install --user "clang-format>=20"` works; then
`export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"`). Use `... --target format` to rewrite in place.
